# <type>(<catalog>): <imperative subject, ~72 chars>
#
# Conventional Commits, in English.
#
# SCOPE is the catalog the change touches (legal scopes are the catalogs
# listed in ARCHITECTURE.md), e.g. feat(core): ...
# OMIT the scope when the change touches no catalog — harness, CI, docs,
# tooling: docs: ...
#
# TYPE is chosen by effect on installed behavior, not by file format:
#   feat     adds a capability a target project gets
#   fix      corrects wrong or misleading installed behavior
#   refactor restructures without changing installed behavior
#   docs     supporting docs only; changes no installed skill
#   test     the validator and its self-test fixtures
#   ci       workflows and automation
#   chore    tooling and housekeeping
#
# BODY: explain why, not what. Wrap at 72 characters. No trailers.
#
# Before committing: run `just check`, and read the staged diff yourself
# for secrets and personal data — a secret committed is leaked even if a
# later commit removes it. One logical change per commit.
# Never use --no-verify.
